{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1415011-could-a-virtual-adept-learn-or-possess-technocratic-spheres","id":1415011,"title":"Could a Virtual Adept Learn or Possess Technocratic Spheres?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-21T20:20:03-07:00","id":1415011,"title":"Could a Virtual Adept Learn or Possess Technocratic Spheres?","content":"Here's the question: Although in M20 the book says that you can't possess dimentional science or primal utility if you're a member of the traditions. Could we reasonably say that a former technocrat (now virtual adept) could possess technocratic spheres or is there some mystical restriction? Would he lose those spheres upon conversion? If not would there be any mechanical changes to those sphers in terms of paradigm? And finally how would other members of the Tradions and other Virtual Adepts feel about this? Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26413-thatonekiasyd","name":"ThatOneKiasyd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26413_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T21:05:08-07:00","id":1415014,"title":"","content":"Learn no, but I would say someone who was a defecting technocrat who joined the VA could start with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T04:52:35-07:00","id":1415042,"title":"","content":"That.<br /> <br /> Except for Data. VA can learn Data, they invented it after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T05:06:00-07:00","id":1415043,"title":"","content":"I would definataly give a hard pass about dimensional science because the technocratic idea is so different from the mythical and the VA mindset. The VA have a problem with the idea of spirits and there streetshamans are more like those from Shadowrun where you ask yourself, if he smoke some good stuff, his mind shifting his vision to make it fit or if he really is talking with a conscioness lightbulp. Another thing is for the VA there the believing that everything is in this dimension because if there are other dimension it means that they have no chance to ever reach ascension because it is already hard enough to make their math working on this dimension. Another dimension with other constants makes it actually impossible to use their magic their because then they need to figure out the sourcecode their and mayby never actually being able to look at the real source but only the finished closed endproducts.<br /> For them everything going through different space and dimension is actually just using a cheat code to port you somewhere else in the game. Their internet is more like the Delamar Matrix from the fifth edition in SR. Not just a conncection of hosts and servers but the real origin flow of information.<br /> <br /> I would say something different from developing further primal utility. Because the Syndicate believes that there is some byproduct of happy people creating or selling/buying something which can be interpreted like the will of the market. A defecting Syndicatler can now as VA mayby trying to analyze why exactly something works like this and why it mayby is getting sold. So he has some data to work with there why the primeenergy is created through people buying and selling. Because VA totally believe in prime<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T08:35:11-07:00","id":1415073,"title":"","content":"I thought the spheres are the same, the difference between them is a matter of perspective","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T11:09:50-07:00","id":1415089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1415011-could-a-virtual-adept-learn-or-possess-technocratic-spheres?p=1415073#post1415073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the spheres are the same, the difference between them is a matter of perspective</div> </div> </div> </div>No it is really they have different rules with somewhat different effects.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T11:15:41-07:00","id":1415090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1415011-could-a-virtual-adept-learn-or-possess-technocratic-spheres?p=1415073#post1415073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the spheres are the same, the difference between them is a matter of perspective</div> </div> </div> </div>M20 does state that the original idea was that the Traditions and the Technocracy believe that their mojo it's different, but in truth they're doing the same thing. A sort of meta-joke<br /> <br /> However, the fact of the matter (and this is something M20 aknowledges in the same place) it's that the latest Technocracy books (Convention books of NWO and foward) introduced Spheres with mechanical differences.<br /> <br /> You could say, metaphysically, that these differences arise IOC from &quot;a different perspective&quot;, but ultimately they're not the same","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T19:05:35-07:00","id":1415259,"title":"","content":"So they are different? That just makes thing even more confusing. And ascensions magic system doesn't need to be more confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 09-23-2020, 10:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T23:48:21-07:00","id":1415270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1415011-could-a-virtual-adept-learn-or-possess-technocratic-spheres?p=1415259#post1415259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So they are different? That just makes thing even more confusing. And ascensions magic system doesn't need to be more confusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they are. The Syndicatler for example can easily trade quintessence for Money from &quot;nothing&quot; but in trade they need for getting quintessence all the time investing in some buiseness. If they for example own a small store and really need money right now but they can not afford to use their finances they use the primal utility so the store have somehow some financial boost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T05:18:05-07:00","id":1415290,"title":"","content":"They're just an alternative lens for viewing one of the normal spheres. Though, personally I'm not fond of Primal Utility.<br /> <br /> I would even allow someone with the appropriate paradigm to do the same things with the regular spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T04:30:09-07:00","id":1415394,"title":"","content":"The Technocratic Spheres require a certain mindset to learn, and are thus gated by one's Focus. (Each one specifies what the required mindset is; for instance, Primal Utility is tied to Hyper-economics.) They differ from the regular Spheres in that they do some things better and other things worse: sticking with Primal Utility, it's better at making Wonders and for collecting Quintessence for that purpose (including access to human activity as a source of Quintessence), but it's not so good at treating Quintessence as a kind of energy or substance (e.g., \u201cblades of light\u201d, astral \u201cbodies\u201d, etc.). <br /> <br /> There are actually <i>two</i> Correspondence variants available to the Technocracy: Data and Void Correspondence. The former concentrates on the \u201cconnections\u201d aspect of Correspondence, and essentially requires some sort of \u201cEverything is Data\u201d Paradigm to study, while the latter (which only appears in the Revised Void Engineers Convention Book) focuses more on the Sphere's spatial aspects. The two are rather complementary in nature, with Data not being so good with the Spatial stuff and Void Correspondence not being so good with the information stuff (as a house rule, I say that Void Correspondence, which I rename as \u201cSpace\u201d, can't be used to access the Digital Web). <br /> <br /> I've got a few threads on this topic: <br /> <br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385360-fields-for-the-technocracy-reloaded\"> Fields for the Technocracy</a> takes the Sphere variants to their logically extreme and posit the notion that the Technocracy has its own set of \u201cSpheres\u201d that almost, but don't quite, parallel the nine Spheres that the Traditions pioneered. <br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/88705-sphere-variants-for-the-traditions\"> Sphere Variants for the Traditions</a> is based on the notion that the concept of variants on the Spheres is actually more suitable to the Traditions than to the Technocracy, with each Tradition's distinct Focus giving it special insight into one or two Spheres, such as the Sons of Ether having a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/428316-the-machine-sphere\">Machine Sphere</a> based off of Matter, or the Dreamspeakers having a variant of Spirit that's less about crossing the Gauntlet and visiting other worlds and more about dealing with spiritual entities. <br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/783876-folding-the-technocratic-variants-into-the-regular-spheres\">Restoring the Nine Spheres</a> discusses how the Technocratic variants differ from the Spheres that they're variants of and how to go back to the notion that there are only nine Spheres without losing any of the functionality that the Technocratic variants provide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T08:53:41-07:00","id":1415423,"title":"","content":"IMO, the selling point of the Traditions beyond the other groups is the fluidity of approach and accessibility of knowledge. So I've been house ruling that a suitably technologically inclined Tradition Mage could theoretically learn aspects of Dimensional Science as a specialty, with the appropriate rule variations, while still being open to the more traditional uses of the Spirit sphere (and therefore using &quot;Spirit&quot; as an umbrella term for both.) The Technocrat would not have a parallel option though.<br /> <br /> The character would have to have a pretty good explanation for how he learned the technocratic techniques for me to okay it as a storyteller.<br /> <br /> I go back and forth on Data, because on one hand, I really like the idea and application. But on the other, it feels bizarre to me that the House that occupies the Correspondence seat on the Council doesn't actually use Correspondence. But by using my House Rule, I can kind of reconcile Data as a specialty within the Correspondence sphere as opposed to a replacement. There's probably not much, if any, practical differences between approaches, but it makes me feel better about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T09:26:59-07:00","id":1415427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1415011-could-a-virtual-adept-learn-or-possess-technocratic-spheres?p=1415423#post1415423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO, the selling point of the Traditions beyond the other groups is the fluidity of approach and accessibility of knowledge. So I've been house ruling that a suitably technologically inclined Tradition Mage could theoretically learn aspects of Dimensional Science as a specialty, with the appropriate rule variations, while still being open to the more traditional uses of the Spirit sphere (and therefore using &amp;quot;Spirit&amp;quot; as an umbrella term for both.) The Technocrat would not have a parallel option though.<br /> <br /> The character would have to have a pretty good explanation for how he learned the technocratic techniques for me to okay it as a storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's easy: just accept something along the lines of Tychoidean Cosmology. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1415011-could-a-virtual-adept-learn-or-possess-technocratic-spheres?p=1415423#post1415423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I go back and forth on Data, because on one hand, I really like the idea and application. But on the other, it feels bizarre to me that the House that occupies the Correspondence seat on the Council doesn't actually use Correspondence. But by using my House Rule, I can kind of reconcile Data as a specialty within the Correspondence sphere as opposed to a replacement. There's probably not much, if any, practical differences between approaches, but it makes me feel better about it.</div> </div> </div> </div> My take on it is that the Virtual Adepts developed the Data variant back while they were still part of the Technocracy, but largely abandoned it in favor of Correspondence (which is more flexible, but requires a more mystical perspective) when they left the Union. There are still some holdouts in their table who still practice Data; but they tend to be the exception rather than the rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}